 O₂ → 2CO₂. If 5 L CO reacts with excess O₂, CO₂ formed is:\", \"questionType\": \"multiple_choice\", \"showExplanation\": true, \"questionImageUrl\": null}, {\"id\": \"question-1784888810836-269\", \"title\": \"Question 41\", \"points\": 1, \"choices\": [{\"id\": \"choice-1784888810836-2057\", \"text\": \"1 mole of all gases has same mass\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1784888810836-2058\", \"text\": \"1 mole always has same volume at all conditions\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1784888810836-2059\", \"text\": \"1 mole always contains 6.022×10²³ particles\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": true}, {\"id\": \"choice-1784888810836-2060\", \"text\": \"Mole depends on temperature\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}], \"collapsed\": false, \"explanation\": \"Only Avogadro\'s number is constant definition of mole.\", \"questionText\": \"Which statement is correct?\", \"questionType\": \"multiple_choice\", \"showExplanation\": true, \"questionImageUrl\": null}, {\"id\": \"question-1784888810836-270\", \"title\": \"Question 42\", \"points\": 1, \"choices\": [{\"id\": \"choice-1784888810836-2065\", \"text\": \"Na\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": true}, {\"id\": \"choice-1784888810836-2066\", \"text\": \"Na₂O\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1784888810836-2067\", \"text\": \"Fe₂O₃\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1784888810836-2068\", \"text\": \"None\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}], \"collapsed\": false, \"explanation\": \"Na moles = 230 ÷ 23 = 10 mol. Fe₂O₃ moles = 320 ÷ 160 = 2 mol. Required Na for 2 mol Fe₂O₃ = 12 mol. Only 10 mol Na available → Na is limiting.\", \"questionText\": \"Reaction: 6Na + Fe₂O₃ → 3Na₂O + 2Fe. Limiting reactant is:\", \"questionType\": \"multiple_choice\", \"showExplanation\": true, \"questionImageUrl\": null}, {\"id\": \"question-1784888810836-271\", \"title\": \"Question 43\", \"points\": 1, \"choices\": [{\"id\": \"choice-1784888810836-2073\", \"text\": \"22.4 dm³\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1784888810836-2074\", \"text\": \"44.8 dm³\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": true}, {\"id\": \"choice-1784888810836-2075\", \"text\": \"67.2 dm³\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1784888810836-2076\", \"text\": \"89.6 dm³\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}], \"collapsed\": false, \"explanation\": \"1 mol CH₄ needs 2 mol O₂. 2 mol CH₄ needs 4 mol O₂. 1 mol gas = 22.4 dm³. Volume = 4 × 22.4 = 44.8 dm³.\", \"questionText\": \"CH₄ + 2O₂ → CO₂ + 2H₂O. Oxygen required for methane is:\", \"questionType\": \"multiple_choice\", \"showExplanation\": true, \"questionImageUrl\": null}, {\"id\": \"question-1784888810836-272\", \"title\": \"Question 44\", \"points\": 1, \"choices\": [{\"id\": \"choice-1784888810836-2081\", \"text\": \"900 dm³\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": true}, {\"id\": \"choice-1784888810836-2082\", \"text\": \"1350 dm³\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1784888810836-2083\", \"text\": \"1800 dm³\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1784888810836-2084\", \"text\": \"2700 dm³\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}], \"collapsed\": false, \"explanation\": \"The volume ratio of H₂S to SO₂ is 2:2, which simplifies to 1:1. Therefore, 900 dm³ of H₂S produces 900 dm³ of SO₂ directly by stoichiometric proportion.\", \"questionText\": \"2H₂S + 3O₂ → 2H₂O + 2SO₂. SO₂ production is:\", \"questionType\": \"multiple_choice\", \"showExplanation\": true, \"questionImageUrl\": null}], \"storageKey\": \"13\", \"totalPoints\": 45}',8,5,'2026-07-24 10:26:56','2026-07-24 10:32:15',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-24 10:32:15',8),(9,14,'{\"testId\": 14, \"savedAt\": \"2026-07-24T11:04:03.281Z\", \"version\": 1, \"questions\": [{\"id\": \"question-1784889734624-275\", \"title\": \"Question 1\", \"points\": 1, \"choices\": [{\"id\": \"choice-1