 long-term storage of data?\", \"questionType\": \"multiple_choice\", \"showExplanation\": true, \"questionImageUrl\": null}, {\"id\": \"question-1786994403639-23\", \"title\": \"Question 22\", \"points\": 1, \"choices\": [{\"id\": \"choice-1786994403639-165\", \"text\": \"To increase monitor brightness\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1786994403639-166\", \"text\": \"To connect computers and share resources\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": true}, {\"id\": \"choice-1786994403639-167\", \"text\": \"To replace the CPU\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1786994403639-168\", \"text\": \"To convert electricity into sound\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}], \"collapsed\": false, \"explanation\": \"A computer network connects devices so they can communicate and share data, applications, and resources.\", \"questionText\": \"What is the purpose of a computer network?\", \"questionType\": \"multiple_choice\", \"showExplanation\": true, \"questionImageUrl\": null}], \"storageKey\": \"69\", \"totalPoints\": 20}',1,5,'2026-08-17 19:20:04','2026-08-17 19:21:03',NULL,NULL,'2026-08-17 19:21:03',1),(64,70,'{\"testId\": 70, \"savedAt\": \"2026-08-18T15:47:40.412Z\", \"version\": 1, \"questions\": [{\"id\": \"question-1787068006752-3\", \"title\": \"Question 1\", \"points\": 1, \"choices\": [{\"id\": \"choice-1787068006752-9\", \"text\": \"50 m\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068006752-10\", \"text\": \"100 m\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": true}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068006752-11\", \"text\": \"200 m\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068006752-12\", \"text\": \"400 m\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}], \"collapsed\": false, \"explanation\": \"Average speed = (0 + 20)/2 = 10 m/s. Distance = average speed × time = 10 × 10 = 100 m.\", \"questionText\": \"A car accelerates uniformly from rest to 20 m/s in 10 s. What distance does it cover?\", \"questionType\": \"multiple_choice\", \"showExplanation\": true, \"questionImageUrl\": null}, {\"id\": \"question-1787068006752-4\", \"title\": \"Question 2\", \"points\": 1, \"choices\": [{\"id\": \"choice-1787068006752-17\", \"text\": \"3 J\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068006752-18\", \"text\": \"6 J\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068006752-19\", \"text\": \"9 J\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": true}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068006752-20\", \"text\": \"18 J\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}], \"collapsed\": false, \"explanation\": \"KE = 1/2 mv² = 1/2 × 2 × 3². KE = 9 J.\", \"questionText\": \"A 2 kg object moving at 3 m/s has kinetic energy of:\", \"questionType\": \"multiple_choice\", \"showExplanation\": true, \"questionImageUrl\": null}, {\"id\": \"question-1787068006752-5\", \"title\": \"Question 3\", \"points\": 1, \"choices\": [{\"id\": \"choice-1787068006752-25\", \"text\": \"10 m\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068006752-26\", \"text\": \"20 m\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": true}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068006752-27\", \"text\": \"40 m\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068006752-28\", \"text\": \"80 m\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}], \"collapsed\": false, \"explanation\": \"Using v² = 2gh, 20² = 2 × 10 × h. h = 400/20 = 20 m.\", \"questionText\": \"A ball is thrown vertically upward with speed 20 m/s. Taking g = 10 m/s², the maximum height is:\", \"questionType\": \"multiple_choice\", \"showExplanation\": true, \"questionImageUrl\": null}, {\"id\": \"question-1787068006752-6\", \"title\": \"Question 4\", \"points\": 1, \"choices\": [{\"id\": \"choice-1787068006752-33\", \"text\": \"6 m/s\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068006752-34\", \"text\": \"10 m/s\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-17870680