e pendulum of length 1 m on Earth (g = 10 m/s²) is:\", \"questionType\": \"multiple_choice\", \"showExplanation\": true, \"questionImageUrl\": null}, {\"id\": \"question-1787068006753-19\", \"title\": \"Question 17\", \"points\": 1, \"choices\": [{\"id\": \"choice-1787068006753-137\", \"text\": \"0.25 Hz\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068006753-138\", \"text\": \"2 Hz\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068006753-139\", \"text\": \"4 Hz\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": true}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068006753-140\", \"text\": \"25 Hz\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}], \"collapsed\": false, \"explanation\": \"Frequency f = 1/T = 1/0.25. f = 4 Hz.\", \"questionText\": \"A wave has a period of 0.25 s. Its frequency is:\", \"questionType\": \"multiple_choice\", \"showExplanation\": true, \"questionImageUrl\": null}, {\"id\": \"question-1787068006753-20\", \"title\": \"Question 18\", \"points\": 1, \"choices\": [{\"id\": \"choice-1787068006753-145\", \"text\": \"equilibrium\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068006753-146\", \"text\": \"maximum displacement\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": true}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068006753-147\", \"text\": \"midpoint\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068006753-148\", \"text\": \"zero displacement\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}], \"collapsed\": false, \"explanation\": \"Acceleration in SHM is proportional to displacement from equilibrium. It is maximum at maximum displacement.\", \"questionText\": \"In simple harmonic motion, acceleration is maximum at:\", \"questionType\": \"multiple_choice\", \"showExplanation\": true, \"questionImageUrl\": null}, {\"id\": \"question-1787068006753-21\", \"title\": \"Question 19\", \"points\": 1, \"choices\": [{\"id\": \"choice-1787068006753-153\", \"text\": \"1 J\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": true}, {\"id\": \"choice-178706