f magnetic flux through the coil.\", \"questionText\": \"Induced EMF in a coil depends on the rate of change of:\", \"questionType\": \"multiple_choice\", \"showExplanation\": true, \"questionImageUrl\": null}, {\"id\": \"question-1787068006753-70\", \"title\": \"Question 68\", \"points\": 1, \"choices\": [{\"id\": \"choice-1787068006753-545\", \"text\": \"charge\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068006753-546\", \"text\": \"energy\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": true}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068006753-547\", \"text\": \"momentum\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068006753-548\", \"text\": \"mass\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}], \"collapsed\": false, \"explanation\": \"Induced current opposes the change causing it, ensuring energy is not created. This follows energy conservation.\", \"questionText\": \"Lenz\'s law is a consequence of conservation of:\", \"questionType\": \"multiple_choice\", \"showExplanation\": true, \"questionImageUrl\": null}, {\"id\": \"question-1787068006753-71\", \"title\": \"Question 69\", \"points\": 1, \"choices\": [{\"id\": \"choice-1787068006753-553\", \"text\": \"mutual induction\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": true}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068006753-554\", \"text\": \"self induction only\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068006753-555\", \"text\": \"electrostatic induction\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068006753-556\", \"text\": \"resonance\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}], \"collapsed\": false, \"explanation\": \"Changing current in primary coil induces EMF in secondary coil through mutual induction.\", \"questionText\": \"A transformer operates on the principle of:\", \"questionType\": \"multiple_choice\", \"showExplanation\": true, \"questionImageUrl\": null}, {\"id\": \"question-1787068006753-72\", \"title\": \"Question 70\", \"points\": 1, \"choices\": [{\"i