les.\", \"questionText\": \"The magnetic field lines around a straight current-carrying wire are:\", \"questionType\": \"multiple_choice\", \"showExplanation\": true, \"questionImageUrl\": null}, {\"id\": \"question-1787068059755-167\", \"title\": \"Question 165\", \"points\": 1, \"choices\": [{\"id\": \"choice-1787068059755-1321\", \"text\": \"maximum\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068059755-1322\", \"text\": \"zero\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": true}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068059755-1323\", \"text\": \"infinite\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068059755-1324\", \"text\": \"negative\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}], \"collapsed\": false, \"explanation\": \"F = qvB sinθ. If θ = 0°, sinθ = 0, so magnetic force is zero.\", \"questionText\": \"Magnetic force on a charge moving parallel to a magnetic field is:\", \"questionType\": \"multiple_choice\", \"showExplanation\": true, \"questionImageUrl\": null}, {\"id\": \"question-1787068059755-168\", \"title\": \"Question 166\", \"points\": 1, \"choices\": [{\"id\": \"choice-1787068059755-1329\", \"text\": \"2 N\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068059755-1330\", \"text\": \"4 N\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": true}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068059755-1331\", \"text\": \"8 N\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068059755-1332\", \"text\": \"1 N\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}], \"collapsed\": false, \"explanation\": \"F = BIL = 2 × 4 × 0.5. F = 4 N.\", \"questionText\": \"A 0.5 m wire carrying 4 A is placed perpendicular to a 2 T magnetic field. The force on the wire is:\", \"questionType\": \"multiple_choice\", \"showExplanation\": true, \"questionImageUrl\": null}, {\"id\": \"question-1787068059755-169\", \"title\": \"Question 167\", \"points\": 1, \"choices\": [{\"id\": \"choice-1787068059755-1337\", \"text\": \"electric field\", \"imageUrl\": null, 