5-1395\", \"text\": \"−100°C\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068059755-1396\", \"text\": \"−459°C\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}], \"collapsed\": false, \"explanation\": \"Absolute zero is 0 K, which equals −273.15°C. It is the lowest possible temperature.\", \"questionText\": \"Absolute zero on the Celsius scale is:\", \"questionType\": \"multiple_choice\", \"showExplanation\": true, \"questionImageUrl\": null}, {\"id\": \"question-1787068059755-177\", \"title\": \"Question 175\", \"points\": 1, \"choices\": [{\"id\": \"choice-1787068059755-1401\", \"text\": \"charge\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068059755-1402\", \"text\": \"energy\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": true}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068059755-1403\", \"text\": \"momentum\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068059755-1404\", \"text\": \"entropy\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}], \"collapsed\": false, \"explanation\": \"First law relates heat, work, and internal energy. It is conservation of energy.\", \"questionText\": \"The first law of thermodynamics is a statement of conservation of:\", \"questionType\": \"multiple_choice\", \"showExplanation\": true, \"questionImageUrl\": null}, {\"id\": \"question-1787068059755-178\", \"title\": \"Question 176\", \"points\": 1, \"choices\": [{\"id\": \"choice-1787068059755-1409\", \"text\": \"pressure\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068059755-1410\", \"text\": \"volume\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068059755-1411\", \"text\": \"temperature\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": true}, {\"id\": \"choice-1787068059755-1412\", \"text\": \"heat\", \"imageUrl\": null, \"isCorrect\": false}], \"collapsed\": false, \"explanation\": \"Isothermal means constant temperature. Heat transfer may occur, but temperature does not change.\", \"questionText\": \"In an isothermal